        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "The non-past (or dictionary) form expresses habitual or future actions, while the past form expresses completed actions or past states. For る-Verbs, change the final る to た to form the past tense. Both the non-past and past forms are casual, non-polite forms used in conversation or other grammar patterns.",
